model {
  extend basalt.productionOps {
    metadata {
      constraint "Cloudflare family adoption moves one organization's accounts from the provider ref an app lineage retained across additive scope changes onto the Cloudflare family's canonical provider, which the host derives from its shared declaration. The request names the target ref the consuming apps use, and it must equal that identity. Only a ref whose stored definition derives that identity moves. The exact reviewed account set, generations and active versions must match; a pending sign-in, an acquisition outside the selection or a provider-keyed OAuth client refuses. Account IDs, credentials, generations and links stay; account, version, connection and acquisition provider refs change in one receipt, and every kept link must resolve to the family provider afterwards. The dry run names the apps already on the family ref that start offering the moved accounts, and a test pins the family ref so a declaration change ships with its own adoption. Provider rows are only read."
    }
  }
}
